* dit_cond -- deferred INDIRECT-REFERENCE as a conditional-assignment capture target.
* ORACLE (sbl -bf): "ok dummy=HELLO" -- the match SUCCEEDS and the capture lands in dummy.
* SCRIP: "failed" -- the match FAILS.  Row deferred-indirect-capture-target.
	subject = "HELLO WORLD"
	p = "HELLO" . *$("dummy")
	subject p	:S(ok)F(no)
ok	OUTPUT = "ok dummy=" dummy	:(END)
no	OUTPUT = "failed"
END
